            "summary": "Inspected frozen code at /work/src/multiply.mjs and /work/tests/multiply/behavior.test.mjs read-only. multiply.mjs exports named multiply(a,b): validates both inputs with Number.isSafeInteger (TypeError otherwise), multiplies, validates result with Number.isSafeInteger (RangeError on overflow), returns result; supports zero/negative operands and no implicit coercion. Test file uses node:test + node:assert/strict via dynamic import, covers AC-MUL (multiply(2,3)===6) plus zero, negative, boundary, TypeError (both positions) and positive/negative RangeError overflow. Both files pass node --check. No files modified.",
            "turn_id": "afc9dec0-c40b-4f4d-95f2-a92cc44f606f"
          }
